WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:06.384
"I'll save you!" The prince cried, diving into the water.

2
00:00:06.385 --> 00:00:12.165
He swam as fast as he could to the drowning woman.

3
00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:17.486
He grabbed her and swam back to shore.

4
00:00:17.487 --> 00:00:23.481
"Whew!" The prince gently placed her on the bank of the lake.

5
00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:28.995
But to his shock, she flew up into the air.

6
00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:33.010
"You naughty man!" she yelled down at him.

7
00:00:33.011 --> 00:00:39.150
"Naughty?" the prince said. "You were crying for help!"

8
00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:45.329
"I wasn't crying," the princess said. "I was laughing!"

9
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:51.836
Ellen managed to grab some pinecones from a fir tree.

10
00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:53.918
"Wait till Papa hears about this.

11
00:00:53.919 --> 00:01:00.881
Because of you, I almost floated away!"

12
00:01:00.882 --> 00:01:07.658
She dropped down to the ground and stomped over to the prince.

13
00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:15.309
"Please don't tell him," the prince said. "You seem fine."

14
00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.650
"Why did you pull me out of the water?" Ellen asked.

15
00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:22.835
"I thought you were drowning," the prince said.

16
00:01:22.836 --> 00:01:26.391
She frowned at him. "I might lack gravity.

17
00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:31.065
But it seems you lack something too—brains!"

18
00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:33.980
"It's her!" the prince thought.

19
00:01:33.981 --> 00:01:40.078
People told stories about a light princess with no gravity.

20
00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:42.524
This must be the woman!

21
00:01:42.525 --> 00:01:45.318
The princess stamped her foot.

22
00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:50.757
"I want to go back in the water. You must put me there at once!"

23
00:01:50.758 --> 00:01:56.004
The prince stared into her blue eyes.

24
00:01:56.005 --> 00:02:00.950
"She's beautiful," he thought.

25
00:02:00.951 --> 00:02:04.361
"Did you hear me?" the princess asked.

26
00:02:04.362 --> 00:02:07.952
"I need you to put me back in the water!"

27
00:02:07.953 --> 00:02:10.647
At last the prince understood.

28
00:02:10.648 --> 00:02:15.829
Without gravity, the princess could not put herself back in the water.

29
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:22.876
He took her hand. They walked to another part of the lake.

30
00:02:22.877 --> 00:02:26.145
"How should I put you in the water?" he asked.

31
00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.761
"You pulled me out," she said.

32
00:02:28.762 --> 00:02:39.775
"Please figure out how to put me back!"

33
00:02:39.776 --> 00:02:52.396
"Very well." The prince led her onto a nearby rock.

34
00:02:52.397 --> 00:03:04.363
Then he held her tightly and leaped.

35
00:03:04.364 --> 00:03:10.351
Ellen burst out laughing.

36
00:03:10.352 --> 00:03:17.349
"I never fell into the water like that before. That was so much fun!"

37
00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:27.260
The prince laughed too. "I fell into the water with the most perfect creature ever!"

38
00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:34.176
And away the two of them went, swimming and splashing—and laughing—together.

